// Two-hand actions where the hands touch, overlap or hold one thing together:
// everyday manners and chores, sport, film and stage, and moves seen in games
// and animation that a real body can make. Groundwork for two-hand tracking.
//
// Each key holds both arms, [right, left], in the arm pose key format
// [sFlex, sAbd, hRot, elbow, pron, wFlex, wDev] (armPoses.js, left mirrored).
// The keys were solved, not typed: for each action the place and facing of
// both palms that the contact needs (palms pressed, fingers interlaced, one
// fist in the other palm, both hands on one stick...) was set, and each arm
// was solved to put its palm there inside ARM_ROM, starting from the closest
// recorded arm poses. A key was kept only when both palms got within 2.5 cm
// and 35 deg of their place, neither arm passed through the body or the head,
// and the forearms did not pass through each other (apart from actions that
// cross them). Targets past arm's length are taken at full reach. Each action
// comes at its usual place and moved higher, lower, nearer, farther, right
// and left, where the arms allow it (scratchpad v70/gen.mjs).
//
// Row: [id, name, category, contact, right hand gesture id, left hand gesture id, keys]

